# CODEOWNERS — repository paths → owning engineering roles.
#
# Source of truth: engineering-operating-system/ModuleOwnership.md §1 (ownership map) and §4
# (Phase-0 CODEOWNERS content). Semantics: GitHub CODEOWNERS is LAST-MATCH-WINS, so more specific
# paths appear AFTER their parent rules (RepositoryRules.md §7.3). Every path matches at least one
# rule so the `codeowners-coverage` check passes (ModuleOwnership §6.1; RepositoryRules §7.4).
#
# Team aliases `@eip/r-<xx>` are the lower-cased role IDs from ModuleOwnership §1 / AIAgentCatalog;
# membership (which agent/human holds each role) is administered by the human repository owner
# (ModuleOwnership §7). R-CR is deliberately absent — R-CR reviews every PR as a separately enforced
# required review, never via CODEOWNERS (ModuleOwnership §4 note 1). R-SA is not path-mapped —
# security review routes by change class (CC-2 → G3 + R-SA sign-off), because security-relevant
# diffs cross paths (ModuleOwnership §4 note 2).
#
# Reconciliations recorded in work/tasks/TASK-0007.md:
#  - Location: this file is at .github/CODEOWNERS (task instruction); ModuleOwnership §4 note 3 /
#    RepositoryRules §7.1 name the repo root. GitHub honors both identically; path mappings are
#    unaffected. Flagged for R-CA (the CODEOWNERS-change approver, RepositoryRules §7.5).
#  - Ordering: §4's listed order places /docs/adr/ before /docs/, which under last-match-wins would
#    misassign ADRs to R-DE. Reordered general→specific per RepositoryRules §7.3 to honor §1's map.
#  - Coverage: /program, /sprints, /reviews and the loose root files were added after §4 was
#    written; they are owned here per the §1 principles (program/sprint state → R-TPM; architecture
#    readiness reviews → R-CA). The `*` default encodes the §6.3 "ambiguous → R-CA" rule.

